    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d158">

                <pb facs="0361" n="241" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg241"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.A15A4/1187: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Chairman of the American Delegation
                            (Gibson) to the
                            Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-06-28T13:00:00+01:00">June 28, 1932—1
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received June 28—9:27 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>281. Mr. Kellogg is in Paris. He has given
                    some thought to paying a very brief visit to Geneva but feels it indelicate to
                    do so unless you approve.</p>
                <p>We feel that his presence here for a short visit now would be highly useful as he
                    is enthusiastic about the President’s proposal and his prestige would carry his
                    comments to a wide public especially in Europe. We think a useful purpose would
                    be served in his coming provided you can see no danger attached thereto.</p>
                <p>Will you please instruct as urgently as possible so that we may inform Mr.
                        Kellogg in Paris advisedly if
                    possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gibson</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
